    "summary": "Acoustic gems, explosive Cryptical→Cosmic Charlie, epic Other One",
    "blurb": "The night opens with a folk‑high acoustic set featuring Friend Of The Devil and Dire Wolf before exploding into an electric second half anchored by the soaring Cryptical Envelopment → Cosmic Charlie suite and a marathon Other One. Jerry’s guitar tone shines throughout, and the band delivers tight, adventurous playing from start to finish.",
    "review": "May 2, 1970 at Harpur College captures the Dead in top form. The first set rolls out an intimate acoustic program – Don’t Ease Me In, I Know You Rider, Friend Of The Devil, Dire Wolf and a swinging Cumberland Blues – that many fans describe as a “folk‑high point.” When the electric side kicks in, the band builds momentum into one of the era’s most celebrated sequences: Cryptical Envelopment segues flawlessly into Cosmic Charlie, with Jerry Garcia’s soaring tone and improvisational fire lighting up the room. The Other One follows, turning into an extended, transcendent jam that showcases the group’s telepathic interplay. Highlights continue through a rousing Casey Jones, two takes of Good Lovin’, and a heartfelt Morning Dew that segues into a blistering Viola Lee Blues before winding down with Feedback and a gentle good‑night farewell. Across all available tapes the performance is consistently praised; the Miller soundboard (gd1970-05-02.138227.sbd.miller.flac1648) offers crystal‑clear audio, while the Bear SBD (gd1970-05-02.sbd.BEAR.gems.108673.flac24) provides a solid, complete capture despite occasional low‑bass quirks.",
